# Line endings: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This repo is mounted by Hermes on Windows, Linux, macOS and WSL2, and it ships
# executable scripts. A CRLF shebang (`#!/usr/bin/env python3\r`) fails on Linux and
# WSL2 with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env python3^M", so the repository must not
# carry CRLF — not even when it is committed from a Windows machine with
# core.autocrlf=true, which is what silently produced CRLF here before.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout is byte-identical to a
# Linux one. Skills are text; nothing here needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets, in case a skill ever ships one — never line-ending-converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.mp3  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
